# Machine data and big binaries stay out of git (see README). texts/ IS tracked:
# plain-text stories are content, not data. Anchor to the root runtime data dir
# (users/*.jsonl) -- an unanchored `data/` also swallows web/js/data/, which is
# tracked content (the word/sentence pools the game is built from).
/data/
media/*
!media/.gitkeep
__pycache__/
web/assets/lexar/

# built Go binary
thai-typing-go

# the UI bundle: deno builds web/app.js from web/src/*.ts (see install.sh)
web/app.js

# the deepcut word splitter's venv: ~2.4 GB of TensorFlow, opt-in, rebuilt by
# tools/setup-deepcut.sh (segment.go falls back to the browser without it)
/.venv-deepcut/
